    "priceNumeric": 15000,
    "description": "PNOZ X3 Safety Relay is a highly reliable and widely used safety monitoring device designed for industrial automation systems. It is used for monitoring emergency stop (E-STOP) circuits, safety gates, limit switches, and other safety-related control functions to ensure safe operation of machinery. This safety relay provides fail-safe protection by instantly interrupting the control circuit in case of any fault or hazardous condition. It supports both single-channel and dual-channel input wiring with built-in short circuit and fault detection, ensuring high safety performance in critical applications. (Pilz) The relay is equipped with 3 normally open (NO) safety contacts and 1 normally closed (NC) auxiliary contact, making it suitable for multiple control outputs. Its self-monitoring redundant circuit design ensures reliable operation even in case of internal component failure. (RS Online) 🔹 Key Features Suitable for E-stop, safety gate & interlock monitoring Single & dual-channel operation with cross-fault detection 3 NO safety outputs + 1 NC auxiliary output Automatic or monitored manual reset LED indicators for power and channel status Self-monitoring (fail-safe) design Standard DIN rail mounting (RS Online) 🔹 Applications Industrial machinery safety systems Conveyor & packaging machines CNC and process automation Safety gate and door monitoring Light barriers / safety sensors 🔹 Technical",
